description: Keep the WhatsApp core channel isolated from inbox/CRM features
alwaysApply: true
---

# Two-layer architecture

The product has a **core WhatsApp channel** and an **inbox layer** on top of it. Changing agents, assignment, login UX, notes, or filters must not rewrite send/receive/QR logic.

## Core layer (do not break)

WhatsApp login (QR / linked device), connection state, send, receive, JID/LID handling, and provider adapters.

- Backend: `backend/src/core/`
- Frontend: `frontend/src/channel/`
- HTTP: `/webhook/whatsapp`, `/api/connections`, send path via `sendWhatsAppText`

**`backend/src/core` must never import from `backend/src/inbox`.**

Inbox code must send and receive only through `backend/src/core` (`sendWhatsAppText`, `parseIncomingWhatsApp`, connection helpers). Do not call Evolution/Demo providers from inbox.

## Inbox layer (safe to change)

Agent login, creating/listing agents, assigning/claiming/locking chats, internal notes, conversation list filters.

- Backend: `backend/src/inbox/`
- Frontend: `frontend/src/inbox/`
- HTTP: `/api/auth`, `/api/conversations` (except the actual WhatsApp send, which calls core)

When adding inbox features, persist and display around core events. Do not fork a second WhatsApp client or duplicate webhook parsing.
